# Cell boundaries never overlap

On one section, the area enclosed by one cell's outline belongs to that cell alone. Outlines of two different cells
(structures with different `ParentID`) never overlap, whoever drew them: pen, Segment, auto-polygonize, a move, a
contour change, a paint-mask accept, a merge.

## What follows
- **Existing annotations win.** A new or edited outline is clipped against every other cell's polygon and circle disk on
  that section (`AutoPolygonizeSelection.SubtractOverlappingPolygons`, `CollectOverlappingCircleDisks`). The other cell is
  never the one that gives way, however strong the new outline's evidence is.
- **Same cell is exempt.** Locations of one structure on one section may overlap; they are merged into one outline
  (`SameStructureMerge`), not clipped against each other. Child structures and their parent are not "other cells"
  (`IsRelatedStructure`).
- **Pending outlines follow the store.** A proposal on screen is a claim on area, so it is re-clipped whenever a saved
  location of another cell changes its geometry (a pen refinement, a move, a delete), not only when a proposal is accepted.
  A proposal that was clipped by an outline that has since shrunk grows back from its stored mask; one that has no mask
  can only be clipped further.
- **Clip from the unclipped source.** Re-clipping starts from the traced mask (`MaskSources`), never from an already
  clipped ring, or a region that was given back is lost.
- **No "keep it anyway" exceptions** that leave two cells overlapping. A clip that would leave nothing removes the
  proposal; it does not fall back to the overlapping outline.

## Checklist when adding a path that writes an outline
Does it clip against the other cells before saving? Does it re-clip pending outlines after saving? Does it work from the
volume geometry the user sees (`annotation-volume-geometry.mdc`) and save mosaic? A new view or command that skips the
clip is a bug even when the overlap is small.
